.TH LEADER 1 "" "Leader" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
leader \- Neovim with the Leader config: nvim in a terminal, its own GPU window from the menu
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B leader
[\-\-gui] [\fINEOVIM ARGUMENTS\fR...]
.br
.B leader \-\-help
|
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B leader
is the Leader editor: Neovim with Leader's configuration.
.PP
In a terminal (stdin or stdout is a TTY) it is
.BR nvim
itself: it replaces its own process with Neovim, so every argument goes to Neovim exactly as typed, with the same
terminal, job control and exit code. A launch without a terminal (the applications menu) opens Neovim drawn by the GPU
in a native window with its own app bar, menus, command palette and project picker.
.B \-\-gui
(and \fBLEADER_GUI=1\fR) forces the window even from a terminal. Everything after the command name goes to Neovim, so
files, \fB+cmd\fR and \fB\-d\fR work as usual in both.
.PP
The first launch without any Neovim configuration runs
.BR leader\-setup (1)
in the window itself, which installs Leader's config.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LEADER_NVIM
The Neovim binary to run (default: nvim on PATH).
.TP
.B LEADER_GUI
Always open the GPU window, even in a terminal (same as \-\-gui).
.TP
.B LEADER_FONT
Font before the config sets guifont, e.g. "Iosevka:h13".
.TP
.B LEADER_TIMING
Print startup timings to stderr.
.TP
.B WGPU_BACKEND
Force a GPU backend (vulkan, gl).
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B F10
App menu.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+P
Command palette.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+O
Open a project.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+N
New window.
.TP
.B F11
Fullscreen.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+W
Welcome and install checks.
.TP
.B Ctrl+= / \- / 0
Font size.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/nvim
Leader's configuration (installed by leader\-setup).
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/leader/window
The window's remembered size, place and maximized state.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR leader\-setup (1),
.BR nvim (1)
.PP
https://sazardev.github.io/leader/
